  "id": "cortical-potential",
  "term": "cortical potential",
  "definition": "In this source, a cortical potential is a measurable pattern of the brain cortex’s electrical activity linked to cognitive and motor processing during a task. Here it is discussed specifically as motor-related cortical potential, meaning activity seen around a movement response, including changes before and after the response.",
